# Tests — Annex C annual leave accrual (C-9)

Assertion-based tests for `Leave_accrual`. Three things in C-9 can only be got
wrong silently, and each has its own group of tests here.

The first is the boundary between C-9.1 and C-9.2: a month is either completed
or it is not, and the tests check the day either side of both ends of a month.
The second is C-9.2's denominator, which is the number of days in the month
under examination and not a constant: February 2023, February 2024, a 30-day
month and a 31-day month are all tested, including a pair that differ only in
the leap day and accrue different amounts because of it. The third is C-9.2's
rounding proviso, which is tested directly against `HalfDayRounding` at every
exact quarter and on both sides of every one of them, because the exact
quarter is unreachable through `MonthlyAccrual` (see the module) and would
otherwise never be executed at all.

Counterexamples found by the adversarial reviewer are kept separately, in
`tests/counterexamples/`, and are re-run by `scripts/check.sh`.

> Using LeaveAccrual as LA

## Rounding_Zero

C-9.2: nothing rounds to nothing.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRounding_Zero:
  output r content LA.HalfDayRounding

scope TestRounding_Zero:
  definition r equals output of LA.HalfDayRounding with { -- raw_days: 0.0 }
  assertion r.is_exact_quarter = false
  assertion r.rounded_days = 0.0
```

## Rounding_ExactQuarter_0_25

C-9.2's proviso, the case it was written for: an exact quarter of a day is
exactly midway between nothing and half a day, and it rounds upwards.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRounding_ExactQuarter_0_25:
  output r content LA.HalfDayRounding

scope TestRounding_ExactQuarter_0_25:
  definition r equals output of LA.HalfDayRounding with { -- raw_days: 0.25 }
  assertion r.is_exact_quarter = true
  assertion r.rounded_days = 0.5
```

## Rounding_JustBelowQuarter_0_24

C-9.2: below the quarter the nearest half day is nothing, so the proviso does
not apply and nothing accrues. This is the exact quarter from below.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRounding_JustBelowQuarter_0_24:
  output r content LA.HalfDayRounding

scope TestRounding_JustBelowQuarter_0_24:
  definition r equals output of LA.HalfDayRounding with { -- raw_days: 0.24 }
  assertion r.is_exact_quarter = false
  assertion r.rounded_days = 0.0
```

## Rounding_JustAboveQuarter_0_26

C-9.2: above the quarter the nearest half day is half a day, which is the same
answer the proviso gives, but by the rule and not by the proviso.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRounding_JustAboveQuarter_0_26:
  output r content LA.HalfDayRounding

scope TestRounding_JustAboveQuarter_0_26:
  definition r equals output of LA.HalfDayRounding with { -- raw_days: 0.26 }
  assertion r.is_exact_quarter = false
  assertion r.rounded_days = 0.5
```

## Rounding_ExactQuarter_0_75

C-9.2's proviso at the second quarter. 0.75 is an exact quarter of a day and
is exactly midway between half a day and a whole day, so it rounds upwards to
1.0. The reading that treats only 0.25 as 'an exact quarter' would leave this
value with no rule at all.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRounding_ExactQuarter_0_75:
  output r content LA.HalfDayRounding

scope TestRounding_ExactQuarter_0_75:
  definition r equals output of LA.HalfDayRounding with { -- raw_days: 0.75 }
  assertion r.is_exact_quarter = true
  assertion r.rounded_days = 1.0
```

## Rounding_JustBelow_0_75

C-9.2: the second quarter from below.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRounding_JustBelow_0_75:
  output r content LA.HalfDayRounding

scope TestRounding_JustBelow_0_75:
  definition r equals output of LA.HalfDayRounding with { -- raw_days: 0.74 }
  assertion r.is_exact_quarter = false
  assertion r.rounded_days = 0.5
```

## Rounding_JustAbove_0_75

C-9.2: the second quarter from above.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRounding_JustAbove_0_75:
  output r content LA.HalfDayRounding

scope TestRounding_JustAbove_0_75:
  definition r equals output of LA.HalfDayRounding with { -- raw_days: 0.76 }
  assertion r.is_exact_quarter = false
  assertion r.rounded_days = 1.0
```

## Rounding_ExactQuarter_1_25

C-9.2's proviso at the third quarter.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRounding_ExactQuarter_1_25:
  output r content LA.HalfDayRounding

scope TestRounding_ExactQuarter_1_25:
  definition r equals output of LA.HalfDayRounding with { -- raw_days: 1.25 }
  assertion r.is_exact_quarter = true
  assertion r.rounded_days = 1.5
```

## Rounding_ExactQuarter_1_75

C-9.2's proviso at the fourth quarter, which rounds up to the full monthly
accrual of C-9.1.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRounding_ExactQuarter_1_75:
  output r content LA.HalfDayRounding

scope TestRounding_ExactQuarter_1_75:
  definition r equals output of LA.HalfDayRounding with { -- raw_days: 1.75 }
  assertion r.is_exact_quarter = true
  assertion r.rounded_days = 2.0
```

## Rounding_ExactHalf

C-9.2: an exact half day is already a half day and is not an exact quarter, so
the proviso does not touch it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRounding_ExactHalf:
  output r content LA.HalfDayRounding

scope TestRounding_ExactHalf:
  definition r equals output of LA.HalfDayRounding with { -- raw_days: 0.5 }
  assertion r.is_exact_quarter = false
  assertion r.rounded_days = 0.5
```

## Rounding_ExactTwoDays

C-9.2: the top of the range a month can produce is unchanged by rounding.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRounding_ExactTwoDays:
  output r content LA.HalfDayRounding

scope TestRounding_ExactTwoDays:
  definition r equals output of LA.HalfDayRounding with { -- raw_days: 2.0 }
  assertion r.is_exact_quarter = false
  assertion r.rounded_days = 2.0
```

## C9_1_CompletedMonthMidService

C-9.1: a month falling wholly within an open-ended engagement is a completed
calendar month and accrues 2.0 days.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_1_CompletedMonthMidService:
  output r content LA.MonthlyAccrual

scope TestC9_1_CompletedMonthMidService:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.MonthlyAccrual with {
      -- day_in_month: |2024-01-15|
      -- service_start: |2023-06-01|
      -- service_end: Absent
    }
  assertion r.days_in_month = 31
  assertion r.days_of_service_in_month = 31
  assertion r.month_is_completed = true
  assertion r.days_accrued = 2.0
```

## C9_1_CompletedMonthExactlyCovered

C-9.1: service beginning on the first day and ending on the last day of the
month completes it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_1_CompletedMonthExactlyCovered:
  output r content LA.MonthlyAccrual

scope TestC9_1_CompletedMonthExactlyCovered:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.MonthlyAccrual with {
      -- day_in_month: |2024-01-01|
      -- service_start: |2024-01-01|
      -- service_end: Present content |2024-01-31|
    }
  assertion r.days_of_service_in_month = 31
  assertion r.month_is_completed = true
  assertion r.days_accrued = 2.0
```

## C9_1_CompletedLeapFebruary

C-9.1: a completed February in a leap year accrues 2.0 days like any other
completed month, but only if service covers the 29th.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_1_CompletedLeapFebruary:
  output r content LA.MonthlyAccrual

scope TestC9_1_CompletedLeapFebruary:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.MonthlyAccrual with {
      -- day_in_month: |2024-02-10|
      -- service_start: |2024-02-01|
      -- service_end: Present content |2024-02-29|
    }
  assertion r.days_in_month = 29
  assertion r.days_of_service_in_month = 29
  assertion r.month_is_completed = true
  assertion r.days_accrued = 2.0
```

## C9_1_StartOneDayLateIsNotCompleted

The C-9.1/C-9.2 boundary from the commencement side. Service beginning on the
second day of the month leaves the month uncompleted, so the accrual is
C-9.2's pro-rated figure and not C-9.1's 2.0 days — even though the pro-rated
figure happens to round back to 2.0.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_1_StartOneDayLateIsNotCompleted:
  output r content LA.MonthlyAccrual

scope TestC9_1_StartOneDayLateIsNotCompleted:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.MonthlyAccrual with {
      -- day_in_month: |2024-01-15|
      -- service_start: |2024-01-02|
      -- service_end: Absent
    }
  assertion r.days_of_service_in_month = 30
  assertion r.month_is_completed = false
  assertion r.pro_rated_days = 2.0
  assertion r.days_accrued = 2.0
```

## C9_1_EndOneDayEarlyIsNotCompleted

The same boundary from the termination side.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_1_EndOneDayEarlyIsNotCompleted:
  output r content LA.MonthlyAccrual

scope TestC9_1_EndOneDayEarlyIsNotCompleted:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.MonthlyAccrual with {
      -- day_in_month: |2024-01-15|
      -- service_start: |2023-06-01|
      -- service_end: Present content |2024-01-30|
    }
  assertion r.days_of_service_in_month = 30
  assertion r.month_is_completed = false
  assertion r.days_accrued = 2.0
```

## C9_2_ThirtyOneDayDenominator

C-9.2: twelve days of service in a 31-day month. 2.0 x 12/31 is 0.774..., whose
nearest half day is 1.0.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_2_ThirtyOneDayDenominator:
  output r content LA.MonthlyAccrual

scope TestC9_2_ThirtyOneDayDenominator:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.MonthlyAccrual with {
      -- day_in_month: |2024-01-01|
      -- service_start: |2024-01-20|
      -- service_end: Absent
    }
  assertion r.days_in_month = 31
  assertion r.days_of_service_in_month = 12
  assertion r.month_is_completed = false
  assertion r.days_accrued = 1.0
```

## C9_2_ThirtyDayDenominator

C-9.2: commencing on the 20th of a 30-day month instead. Eleven days of
service out of 30 is 0.733..., whose nearest half day is 0.5 — half the answer
the 31-day month gives for the same day of the month. The denominator is the
days in that month and is not a constant.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_2_ThirtyDayDenominator:
  output r content LA.MonthlyAccrual

scope TestC9_2_ThirtyDayDenominator:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.MonthlyAccrual with {
      -- day_in_month: |2024-04-01|
      -- service_start: |2024-04-20|
      -- service_end: Absent
    }
  assertion r.days_in_month = 30
  assertion r.days_of_service_in_month = 11
  assertion r.month_is_completed = false
  assertion r.days_accrued = 0.5
```

## C9_2_TwentyEightDayDenominator

C-9.2 in a non-leap February. Eighteen days of service out of 28 is 1.285...,
whose nearest half day is 1.5.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_2_TwentyEightDayDenominator:
  output r content LA.MonthlyAccrual

scope TestC9_2_TwentyEightDayDenominator:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.MonthlyAccrual with {
      -- day_in_month: |2023-02-01|
      -- service_start: |2023-02-11|
      -- service_end: Present content |2023-02-28|
    }
  assertion r.days_in_month = 28
  assertion r.days_of_service_in_month = 18
  assertion r.month_is_completed = false
  assertion r.days_accrued = 1.5
```

## C9_2_TwentyNineDayDenominator

C-9.2 in a leap February, on exactly the same dates and exactly the same
eighteen days of service. Eighteen days out of 29 is 1.241..., whose nearest
half day is 1.0. The leap day alone changes the entitlement from 1.5 days to
1.0, which is what a constant denominator would get wrong.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_2_TwentyNineDayDenominator:
  output r content LA.MonthlyAccrual

scope TestC9_2_TwentyNineDayDenominator:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.MonthlyAccrual with {
      -- day_in_month: |2024-02-01|
      -- service_start: |2024-02-11|
      -- service_end: Present content |2024-02-28|
    }
  assertion r.days_in_month = 29
  assertion r.days_of_service_in_month = 18
  assertion r.month_is_completed = false
  assertion r.days_accrued = 1.0
```

## C9_2_LeapDayLeavesMonthUncompleted

C-9.1 against C-9.2 across the leap day. Service from 1 to 28 February
completes the month in 2023 and accrues under C-9.1; the identical dates in
2024 stop one day short of the month's end, so the month is not completed and
the accrual comes from C-9.2 instead.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_2_LeapDayLeavesMonthUncompleted:
  output r content LA.MonthlyAccrual

scope TestC9_2_LeapDayLeavesMonthUncompleted:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.MonthlyAccrual with {
      -- day_in_month: |2024-02-01|
      -- service_start: |2024-02-01|
      -- service_end: Present content |2024-02-28|
    }
  assertion r.days_in_month = 29
  assertion r.days_of_service_in_month = 28
  assertion r.month_is_completed = false
  assertion r.days_accrued = 2.0
```

## C9_1_SameDatesCompleteNonLeapFebruary

The companion to the test above: 1 to 28 February 2023 is a completed calendar
month and accrues under C-9.1.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_1_SameDatesCompleteNonLeapFebruary:
  output r content LA.MonthlyAccrual

scope TestC9_1_SameDatesCompleteNonLeapFebruary:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.MonthlyAccrual with {
      -- day_in_month: |2023-02-01|
      -- service_start: |2023-02-01|
      -- service_end: Present content |2023-02-28|
    }
  assertion r.days_in_month = 28
  assertion r.days_of_service_in_month = 28
  assertion r.month_is_completed = true
  assertion r.days_accrued = 2.0
```

