  assertion r.month_is_completed = false
  assertion r.days_accrued = 1.0
```

## C9_2_TerminationMidMonth

C-9.2 on the termination limb: service ending on the 16th of a 31-day month
gives sixteen days of service and 1.032... days of raw accrual, whose nearest
half day is 1.0.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_2_TerminationMidMonth:
  output r content LA.MonthlyAccrual

scope TestC9_2_TerminationMidMonth:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.MonthlyAccrual with {
      -- day_in_month: |2024-01-01|
      -- service_start: |2023-06-01|
      -- service_end: Present content |2024-01-16|
    }
  assertion r.days_in_month = 31
  assertion r.days_of_service_in_month = 16
  assertion r.month_is_completed = false
  assertion r.days_accrued = 1.0
```

## C9_2_SingleDayOfService

C-9.2: one day of service in a 31-day month is 0.064... days of raw accrual,
whose nearest half day is nothing. A single day of service accrues no leave.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_2_SingleDayOfService:
  output r content LA.MonthlyAccrual

scope TestC9_2_SingleDayOfService:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.MonthlyAccrual with {
      -- day_in_month: |2024-01-01|
      -- service_start: |2024-01-31|
      -- service_end: Absent
    }
  assertion r.days_of_service_in_month = 1
  assertion r.month_is_completed = false
  assertion r.days_accrued = 0.0
```

## C9_2_NoServiceInTheMonth

C-9.2's degenerate case: a month wholly before the engagement begins. The
clause's own words describe commencement and termination, but the arithmetic
it supplies gives zero days of service and so no accrual, which is the only
sensible answer.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_2_NoServiceInTheMonth:
  output r content LA.MonthlyAccrual

scope TestC9_2_NoServiceInTheMonth:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.MonthlyAccrual with {
      -- day_in_month: |2024-01-15|
      -- service_start: |2024-03-01|
      -- service_end: Absent
    }
  assertion r.days_of_service_in_month = 0
  assertion r.month_is_completed = false
  assertion r.days_accrued = 0.0
```

## C9_2_MonthAfterTermination

The same degenerate case on the other side of the engagement.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_2_MonthAfterTermination:
  output r content LA.MonthlyAccrual

scope TestC9_2_MonthAfterTermination:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.MonthlyAccrual with {
      -- day_in_month: |2024-06-15|
      -- service_start: |2023-01-01|
      -- service_end: Present content |2024-03-31|
    }
  assertion r.days_of_service_in_month = 0
  assertion r.month_is_completed = false
  assertion r.days_accrued = 0.0
```

## C9_3_BalanceAboveTheCap

C-9.3: a twelve-day balance carries forward 5 days, and C-9.5 forfeits the
other 7, which are not payable on termination.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_3_BalanceAboveTheCap:
  output r content LA.CarryForward

scope TestC9_3_BalanceAboveTheCap:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.CarryForward with {
      -- accrued_untaken_days: 12.0
      -- prevented_from_taking_leave_by_long_term_sickness: false
    }
  assertion r.permitted_carry_forward_days = 5.0
  assertion r.carry_forward_days = 5.0
  assertion r.forfeited_days = 7.0
  assertion r.forfeited_days_payable_on_termination = false
```

## C9_4_BalanceAboveTheCapWithLongTermSickness

C-9.4 on the same twelve-day balance: the permitted amount becomes the whole
balance, all 12 days carry forward, and C-9.5 forfeits nothing. This is the
interaction the exception exists for, and it is the pair to the test above.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_4_BalanceAboveTheCapWithLongTermSickness:
  output r content LA.CarryForward

scope TestC9_4_BalanceAboveTheCapWithLongTermSickness:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.CarryForward with {
      -- accrued_untaken_days: 12.0
      -- prevented_from_taking_leave_by_long_term_sickness: true
    }
  assertion r.permitted_carry_forward_days = 12.0
  assertion r.carry_forward_days = 12.0
  assertion r.forfeited_days = 0.0
  assertion r.forfeited_days_payable_on_termination = false
```

## C9_3_BalanceExactlyAtTheCap

C-9.3: 'a maximum of 5' includes 5, so a five-day balance carries forward
whole. This is the cap from on top of it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestC9_3_BalanceExactlyAtTheCap:
  output r content LA.CarryForward

scope TestC9_3_BalanceExactlyAtTheCap:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.CarryForward with {
      -- accrued_untaken_days: 5.0
      -- prevented_from_taking_leave_by_long_term_sickness: false
    }
  assertion r.carry_forward_days = 5.0
  assertion r.forfeited_days = 0.0
```

## C9_3_BalanceJustBelowTheCap

C-9.3: the cap from below. Half days are possible balances, because C-9.2
