## InputDomain_C9_2_ServiceEndingOnTheDayItBeganIsTheFloor

The module asserts that `service_end`, where present, is not earlier than
`service_start`: C-9.1 and C-9.2 both measure a period "of service" running
from commencement to termination, and employment cannot terminate before it
commences.

The lawful boundary is a service period of a single day — commencing and
terminating on the same date — which is one day of service in the month and
accrues nothing once C-9.2's pro-rating is rounded to the nearest half day.
`probe.py` reports `AssertionFailed` for a service end date earlier than the
service start date.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestInputDomain_C9_2_ServiceEndingOnTheDayItBeganIsTheFloor:
  output r content LA.MonthlyAccrual

scope TestInputDomain_C9_2_ServiceEndingOnTheDayItBeganIsTheFloor:
  definition r equals
    output of LA.MonthlyAccrual with {
      -- day_in_month: |2025-03-15|
      -- service_start: |2025-03-10|
      -- service_end: Present content |2025-03-10|
    }
  assertion r.days_in_month = 31
  assertion r.days_of_service_in_month = 1
  assertion r.month_is_completed = false
  assertion r.days_accrued = 0.0
```
